<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-3">3 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">USS Vincennes shoots down Iran Air Flight 655</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The US cruiser Vincennes, mistaking the Airbus for an attacking fighter, shot down <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> Air Flight 655 over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>, killing all 290 on board. The tragedy deepened hostility between Washington and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-17">17 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pakistan's President Zia ul-Haq dies in a plane crash</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-zia-ul-haq">Muhammad Zia-ul-Haq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>'s military ruler for eleven years, died when his C-130 crashed near Bahawalpur. The US ambassador also died; the cause has never been established.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-16">16 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Benazir Bhutto's party wins Pakistan's general election</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> Peoples Party, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benazir-bhutto">Benazir Bhutto</a>, won the most seats in the first open election in over a decade. Weeks later she became the first woman to lead a Muslim-majority democracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-21">21 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">A bomb destroys Pan Am Flight 103 over Lockerbie</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A bomb exploded aboard a Boeing 747 over Lockerbie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, killing all 259 on board and 11 people on the ground. A Libyan intelligence officer was convicted in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/johnson-south-reef-skirmish">Johnson South Reef skirmish</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Johnson South Reef skirmish was a naval clash on 14 March 1988 in the Spratly Islands of the South China Sea between Chinese and Vietnamese forces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/1988-armenian-earthquake">1988 Armenian earthquake</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 1988 Armenian earthquake struck northern Soviet Armenia on 7 December 1988 with a magnitude of about 6.8, destroying the town of Spitak and heavily damaging Leninakan, now Gyumri.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-afabet" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-afabet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-afabet">Battle of Afabet</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Afabet was fought in March 1988 around the town of Afabet in northern Eritrea, where the Eritrean People's Liberation Front overran the headquarters of the Ethiopian army's Nadew Command.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/halabja-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halabja-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/halabja-massacre">Halabja massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Halabja massacre was a chemical weapons attack by Iraqi forces on the Kurdish town of Halabja on 16 March 1988, near the end of the Iran–Iraq War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/new-york-accords">New York Accords</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The New York Accords were signed at the United Nations on 22 December 1988 by Angola, Cuba and South Africa.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/matignon-accords-1988">Matignon Accords (1988)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Matignon Accords were signed in June 1988 at the Hôtel Matignon in Paris by the French government of Michel Rocard, the Kanak independence leader Jean-Marie Tjibaou and the loyalist leader Jacques Lafleur.</p></div></li></ol></section>
